<Base title="How this site is run · vikrantsingh.fyi">
  <h1>How this site is run</h1>
  <p>
    A static page on a CDN almost never goes down, so an uptime number for it proves nothing. This site has one small
    dynamic path, so there is something real to operate.
  </p>
  <p>How it works:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>A scheduled job checks this site's latest commit and build status every 10 minutes and stores a snapshot.</li>
    <li>Every page reads that snapshot into the footer. If the read fails, the page still serves without it.</li>
    <li>An external probe checks every 5 minutes that the snapshot is fresh. Two service level objectives sit on those results.</li>
    <li>I break it on purpose, restore it, and write down what I learned. <a href="/notes/postmortem-game-day-1/">Postmortem: game day 1</a> (1 October 2026).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Status: the heartbeat and the external probe have been running since 30 September 2026. The first 30-day SLO numbers come after that window closes.</p>
  <p><a href="/reliability/">See the live reliability dashboard →</a></p>

  <h2>How it's built</h2>
  <p>
    Astro static pages served by one Cloudflare Worker, which also runs the scheduled job, the probe endpoint, an SLI
    ledger in a Durable Object, and the dashboard. Incidents go to a separate engine that runs on GitHub Actions, with
    GitHub Issues as the human gate. Both are public, with every decision written down.
  </p>
